    <dcterms:title>The Fantasy Fan, Volume 1, Number 12, August 1934
The Fan's Own Magazine</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantasy_Fan</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Greg Weeks, Mary Meehan and the Online Distributed Proofreading Team at http://www.pgdp.net</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Fantasy Fan, Volume 1, Number 12, August 1934" by Various is a fan magazine published in August 1934. This issue represents a landmark moment in weird fiction history, part of the first fan magazine devoted to fantasy and horror. Despite its amateur production and tiny circulation of roughly 300 copies, it featured contributions from legendary authors including H.P. Lovecraft, Robert E. Howard, Clark Ashton Smith, and Robert Bloch. The magazine serialized groundbreaking works and fostered spirited debates among the genre's pioneers during its brief but influential eighteen-issue run. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 68.6 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
